Program Bug_2_18_PrivatePublicNoParserSupport;
// Bug 2.18: `private`/`public` are reserved keywords with zero parser
// support. Parser::Record() (parses both `record` and `class` bodies)
// only special-cases PROCEDURE/FUNCTION/INTERRUPT tokens; anything else
// falls through to VariableDeclarations(), which immediately Eat()s
// TokenType::ID. Since PRIVATE/PUBLIC are their own distinct token types
// (not ID), that Eat() fails immediately. There is currently no way to
// mark a class/record member private; every member is effectively
// public.
//
// Method B (compile-time), no VICE step. Confirmed live: this fails with
// "Expected 'ID' but found 'Point_PRIVATE'" (the class-name-prefixed form
// of the PRIVATE token) right where the `private` section starts. Pre-fix
// expected behavior: compile failure with that error. There is no
// known-good variant to fall back on: no configuration of `private`/
// `public` in a record/class body compiles today. Post-fix, once
// Parser::Record() gains real visibility-section handling, this should
// compile clean (or, at minimum, the same construct should no longer be
// a hard parse error).

var
	Point = record
		private
		x, y : byte;
	end;

	p1 : Point;

begin
	p1.x := 10;
	loop();
end.
